  "notes": "{暮|く}らす is an intransitive godan verb meaning to live (lifestyle) or make a living.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜で{暮|く}らす: to live in (place)\n- 〜と{暮|く}らす: to live with (person)\n- 〜で{暮|く}らす: to live on (income)\n- {幸|しあわ}せに{暮|く}らす: to live happily\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {暮|く}らす: lifestyle, how one spends daily life\n- {住|す}む: residence, where one lives (location-focused)\n- {生|い}きる: to be alive, to live (existence)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {暮|く}らし: life, living, livelihood\n- {一人暮|ひとりぐ}らし: living alone\n- {日暮|ひぐ}らし: daily life; day-to-day living\n\nThe ている form {暮|く}らしている describes an ongoing living situation.",
